{"kind":"artifact","text":"The `internal/apphost` package at exact head 8b5dd5ac2f9bd028e2d9aff5a94ad20d645e0be4. It holds the host-binding vocabulary and the repository state around it, moved out of the Workroom-coupled adapter: what a binding record is, who may record one, which one is in force (BindingInForce, answering for one exact named revision rather than re-asking the ref), and what a checkout must remember to reopen its own log (Config, Actor, VerifiedFrontier, LoadConfig, SaveConfig, ResolveGitDirs, MetaDir, ValidateGenesis). It imports no application profile, which is what lets a program that has never heard of Workroom read a binding a Workroom build wrote, and it is what keeps the public `host` package free of layer-5 meaning. The binding read is a bounded pre-audit read, not a verification: it authenticates the initializing actor's signature over an intent naming the genesis and the tree, and leaves the sequencer chain to the audit that runs before any record is folded. This head also carries WriteFileAtomically, moved here from internal/app during the rebase onto de9a2b83 so that SaveConfig and the resident advertisement share one collision-safe implementation at the layer that owns the metadata directory, rather than a copy on each side of the seam. Gates at this exact head: gofmt -l empty, go build ./... clean, go vet ./... clean, go test -count=1 ./... green across all 27 packages.","body":{"commit":"8b5dd5ac2f9bd028e2d9aff5a94ad20d645e0be4","path":"internal/apphost"}}